<title>USA: Court favors Biogen patent extension.</title>
<headline>Court favors Biogen patent extension.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biogen Inc Tuesday said that the European Court of Justice in Luxembourg has ruled in its favor in a lawsuit on issues related to the extension of Biogen's European hepatitis B antigen patents.</p>
<p>As a result, Biogen said it expects that its entire European hepatitis B patent portfolio will be extended for an additional one to five years from the original expiration dates, depending on the market.</p>
<p>Jim Vincent, Biogen's Chairman and Chief Executive Officer, said, &quot;(the decision) ensures that Biogen will continue to receive all of its current European royalties on hepatitis B products into the twenty-first century.&quot;</p>
</text>
